ve_call_896da142fa8e_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_896da142fa8e","agent_id":"main","sequence":85,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_7cbea70050f0_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_7cbea70050f0","agent_id":"main","sequence":87,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_fb605ea7c14d_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_fb605ea7c14d","agent_id":"main","sequence":90,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_122f2c87bf2d","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:19.071240+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:33.935749+00:00","duration_ms":14864.50310004875,"text":"**Refining display figures**\n\nI’m thinking we need to simplify our figure so it's easier to read on screen. Maybe we can create a new static figure with a core map on the left side at 200 high and scatter the math lines on the right, all using 18-point font. I want to ensure users can download it, and I should modify the script to adjust sizes. Axes should remain the same while improving title sizes and captions for clarity. Let's focus on practicality!**Improving map readability**\n\nI think the user wants the right panel to show measurements clearly rather than in microscopic detail. I could adjust the titles to something like \"1 Equal-area projection\" and \"WGS84 → local LAEA metres\" in different sizes for clarity. It seems crucial to balance font readability and layout. I can create a landscape format at 672px height for better proportions. I also need to remove unnecessary x/y labels to enhance visibility and emphasize the equal-area projection. Let's keep adjusting for better readability!","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":92,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_d0dbf291104f_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_d0dbf291104f","agent_id":"main","sequence":93,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_fd0e2e9d4e5c_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_fd0e2e9d4e5c","agent_id":"main","sequence":95,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_4d5a47309b9c","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:53.069813+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:00:55.834724+00:00","duration_ms":2764.9062999989837,"text":"**Planning revisions and fixes**\n\nI need to ensure that I have a PNG view and register revision aligned. I'll also want to focus on fixing the packaging later. It feels like there’s a lot to juggle, but I think breaking it down into these parts will help keep everything organized. It’s a bit challenging, but I’m aiming for clarity and efficiency! Let's make sure everything is in good shape.","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":97,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_374c7f819562_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_374c7f819562","agent_id":"main","sequence":98,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_f736fed2a004_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_f736fed2a004","agent_id":"main","sequence":99,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_acb9148d5a0b","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T07:01:04.498209+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:01:12.656026+00:00","duration_ms":8157.812700141221,"text":"**Organizing packaging scripts**\n\nI’m figuring out some details for the packaging update script. The width exceeds a certain limit, but it fits within expected dimensions. I need to update the surface, inspect, and capture. My plan is to use explicit commands to compress files without removing everything—a cautious approach. I’ll make a portable version of the script, including a README for instructions. The final step will be zipping everything up neatly. This should keep it straightforward and safe!","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":102,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_18392147f017_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_18392147f017","agent_id":"main","sequence":103,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_c6803ec7064e_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_c6803ec7064e","agent_id":"main","sequence":106,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_d06fc8aa235f_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_d06fc8aa235f","agent_id":"main","sequence":108,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_979038efc1c8_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_979038efc1c8","agent_id":"main","sequence":109,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_f88747cea048_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_f88747cea048","agent_id":"main","sequence":112,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_d307c6c4c547","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T07:01:34.677935+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:01:39.814125+00:00","duration_ms":5136.185199953616,"text":"**Finalizing the script**\n\nI need to finish the final tasks. It sounds like I should output a script but without re-running newer changes that aren’t verified. I must check the root changes from the prior check, and I have to cite sources correctly without any markdown or artifact links. The developer wants actual citations, but the tool specifically prohibits them. I’ll focus on creating a report based on the inspected files and include the public TRPA source link in about 400 words, avoiding LaTex to prevent conflicts.**Clarifying the answer**\n\nI can confirm that a valid polygon boundary can be approximated. I need to compute equal areas; the conversion table shows 497.727861, which isn't excessively precise. I'll explain the grid while noting that the source shape area is 498.1368, emphasizing that I should avoid relying solely on raw attributes. It might be useful for educational purposes to mention the differences between 498.1 projected and 497.7. I’ll include a warning about the certainty and unknown physical conditions today. Since a single value prose suffices, there's no need for a metric surface.","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":114,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_12c17d6ce8e9_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_12c17d6ce8e9","agent_id":"main","sequence":115,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_2445c8819410","type":"text","text":"## Yes—as a mapped surface-area estimate\n\nNDP’s Lake Tahoe boundary encloses approximately **497.7 km²**, equivalent to **192.2 square miles** or **123,000 acres**.\n\nI used the Tahoe Regional Planning Agency’s **“Lake Tahoe boundary delineation”** found through NDP—not the watershed, jurisdiction boundary, or separate high-water-line layer. [TRPA source layer](https://maps.trpa.org/server/rest/services/Datadownloader_SoilsandHydro/MapServer/1)\n\nThe interactive map above shows the actual polygon; the annotated map shows how its area was measured. I visually checked both.\n\n### How I measured it\n\n1. **Checked the geometry:** one valid polygon with 20,472 ring coordinates, including the closing coordinate. No smoothing or geometry repair was needed.\n2. **Converted longitude/latitude to metres** using a local **Lambert azimuthal equal-area projection**, centred at 39.1° N, 120° W. Measuring directly in degrees² or from a Web Mercator map would not give a reliable area.\n3. **Calculated the enclosed polygon area:** 497,727,861 m² ÷ 1,000,000 = **497.727861 km²**.\n4. **Cross-checked on Earth’s WGS84 ellipsoid:** the geodesic calculation also gave **497.727861 km²**.\n\nThe grid makes the measurement visible: **429 complete 1 km² squares**, plus **68.728 km² across 143 clipped shoreline squares**, total **497.728 km²**. Partial squares were measured exactly, not rounded up.\n\n### What this boundary cannot establish\n\nThis is **the area inside the mapped boundary, not necessarily today’s water surface**. The inspected metadata does not specify a shoreline survey date, reference water level, or positional accuracy. The polygon also contains no island holes, so I did not independently subtract islands. Close agreement between calculation methods does **not** establish equivalent shoreline accuracy. [Publisher metadata](https://maps.trpa.org/server/rest/services/Datadownloader_SoilsandHydro/MapServer/1/metadata)\n\n**Saved outputs:** `tahoe_area_map.png`, `measured_boundary.geojson`, `measurement_method.md`, and `tahoe_calculation_package.zip` containing the source geometry, metadata, calculations, grid-cell areas, and reproduction script.","agent_id":"main","sequence":117,"stream_source":"live","channel":"answer"},{"id":"part_323afeade382","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_47ed32665c174a5daf93ef98517023fc","agent_id":"main","sequence":118},{"id":"part_58be7eac7cff","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_3a09385d009c4dcb9e1155fc044a5924","agent_id":"main","sequence":119},{"id":"part_9d7390ebdc21","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_22bf7ec3fa6249398f8450df246ba997","agent_id":"main","sequence":120},{"id":"part_63574b17d909","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_d9f5703414c5420b8d52c59e98cbacf4","agent_id":"main","sequence":121}],"run_id":"a359ea79-4c95-4063-89a8-f345ed58c687","usage":{"input":5456958,"output":13640,"cache_read":5032832,"cache_write":0},"stop_reason":"end_turn","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:02:24.086936+00:00"},{"id":"2a8625f6-7d4f-4c6e-953a-06473215e6a3","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","role":"user","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:10:03.627451+00:00","blocks":[{"id":"part_195894464b99","type":"text","text":"How much does the estimated shoreline length depend on map detail? Show a comparison at several resolutions.","channel":"answer"}],"run_id":"2a8625f6-7d4f-4c6e-953a-06473215e6a3","model":{"provider_id":"codex","model_id":"gpt-6.1-sol"},"usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cache_read":0,"cache_write":0}},{"id":"msg_asst_587b3a98be67","session_id"