ool","tool_id":"call_28f7cdb0bac9","agent_id":"main","sequence":38,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_213e25ee1258","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T07:21:46.165972+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:21:56.800620+00:00","duration_ms":10634.639899944887,"text":"**Preparing comparisons and validations**\n\nI'm focusing on user needs, particularly for \"both area and shoreline comparisons.\" I'll look into area comparison methods. I also need to account for logs and warnings, especially about deprecated material, while being honest in the release notes. I'm planning on creating a standalone verifier that checks if files are UTF-8 and GIF-compatible. I noticed the original method file got corrupted during copying, which I need to address. It's crucial to prepare a final package verification report as well.**Finalizing packaging and verification**\n\nI need to avoid shipping duplicate reruns to reduce clutter. For the user, I must ensure the verification_report.json includes stdout and stderr, while also addressing local absolute paths in warnings. The user requested that scripts be portable and without local dependencies. Logs should eliminate any shared workspace paths for privacy, replacing them with placeholders like `[EXTRACTED_PACKAGE]`. I also want to ensure my output reports contain no specific paths. Finally, I'll make sure the final archive includes updated reports, summaries, and manifests for integrity verification.**Updating README and reports**\n\nI need to add a `validation/` section in the README for verifying provenance. I'll recompute the manifest to include sanitized validation documents and logs. The original report mentioned 20 candidates, but the final count is 28 from updated tests. I can package the `validation/first_run.json` report with logs of the tests. It’s essential to include a note about the verification report, confirming that it reflects the original scientific payload. Also, I'll utilize `baseline_test.json` and `VALIDATION.md` for clarity without self-references in the final report.","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":40,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"part_43b0ef2778ab","type":"text","text":"The first clean-extraction test passed. Both analyses ran in an isolated Python environment with offline mode enabled and no CLIO package installed. The rerun matched all 572 grid-cell rows, all ten shoreline-resolution rows, and the output geometry coordinates exactly; both regenerated figures were also pixel-identical on this Windows test host.\n\nI’m adding the test record to the bundle, then checking the final ZIP again so the released package—not just the working folder—is verified.","agent_id":"main","sequence":41,"stream_source":"live","channel":"next_thought"},{"id":"live_call_eb1eb49aa71c_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_eb1eb49aa71c","agent_id":"main","sequence":42,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_c655fc3e42c2_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_c655fc3e42c2","agent_id":"main","sequence":43,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_b3d0e82b5694_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_b3d0e82b5694","agent_id":"main","sequence":44,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_22d986991f1f_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_22d986991f1f","agent_id":"main","sequence":48,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_42b168ebfc7f_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_42b168ebfc7f","agent_id":"main","sequence":50,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_acb981fd08e3","type":"reasoning","started_at":"2026-10-19T07:22:56.781680+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:23:03.834112+00:00","duration_ms":7052.426600130275,"text":"**Considering package requirements**\n\nI'm checking if there are any hardcoded links in the documentation for the \"companion script original job root\" package. It's important that the final GeoJSON method bodies are absolute and it's crucial that the scripts run outside of Windows without needing specific paths. I also need to confirm if the \"lockmd\" packages are the exact versions that work on Mac. Finally, I should prepare a README with the proper Python environment details and test for any intentional file tampering.**Evaluating testing processes**\n\nI'm considering the need for additional tests to ensure the reliability of the scripts and detect failures in a reproducible manner. Although this isn't explicitly requested, it could be helpful in about 30 seconds. For tampering tests, I could modify the source by appending a newline and then verify the hash to ensure it fails before analysis. It’s essential to maintain the integrity of the package and avoid creating duplicates when using extraction routines. I'll also want to capture expected failures clearly.","source":"provider","provider_source":"model","reasoning_source":"provider_field","default_collapsed":true,"agent_id":"main","sequence":52,"stream_source":"live","channel":"provider_thinking:model:provider_field"},{"id":"live_call_0730a0da939d_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_0730a0da939d","agent_id":"main","sequence":53,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_fb79681b2cc7_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_fb79681b2cc7","agent_id":"main","sequence":54,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_de224c21bee3_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_de224c21bee3","agent_id":"main","sequence":57,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"live_call_09fc249eb21d_call","type":"tool","tool_id":"call_09fc249eb21d","agent_id":"main","sequence":59,"stream_source":"live"},{"id":"part_9a56d1de6915","type":"text","text":"**Yes. Both analyses are now packaged to run without CLIO**, and I verified the final ZIP after extracting it into a fresh folder.\n\n### Share these files\n- **`tahoe_reproducibility_bundle.zip`** — 1.34 MB; source boundary, provenance, methods, expected results, figures, portable Python scripts, pinned dependencies and automated checks.\n- **`tahoe_reproducibility_verification.md`** — verification results, package checksum and portability limitations.\n\nThe ZIP includes an offline **`report.html`** so your colleague can view both analyses without running Python.\n\n### Verification results\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| ZIP integrity and source/file checksums | Passed |\n| GeoJSON, CSV, JSON, XML and Python files | Parsed and validated |\n| Figures | Fully decoded and visually inspected |\n| Area analysis rerun | **497.727861 km²**, reproduced |\n| Shoreline comparison rerun | All **10 detail settings** reproduced |\n| Numerical differences in both CSVs | **Zero** |\n| Output geometry coordinate differences | **Zero** |\n| Regenerated figures | Both **pixel-identical** on the test host |\n\nThe final test passed **2,851 automated checks** in an isolated Python environment, with offline mode enabled and no CLIO package installed.\n\n### Colleague’s quick start\n\nExtract the ZIP, enter its `tahoe-reproducibility` folder, then run:\n\n```text\nuv run --isolated --no-project --python 3.14 --with-requirements requirements.lock.txt python verify.py\n```\n\nThe README also provides a pip/virtual-environment option. A successful run prints `\"status\": \"PASS\"` and produces regenerated results, an HTML summary and verification logs.\n\n**Limits:** tested on **Windows 11 with Python 3.14.8**; macOS/Linux and opening files in Excel or QGIS were not tested. First-time dependency installation needs internet access or a prepared package cache; the analyses run offline afterward. The original scientific caveats remain documented in the package.","agent_id":"main","sequence":61,"stream_source":"live","channel":"answer"},{"id":"part_c01c982029f0","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_97071404627145fe8fe181910c25e8e9","agent_id":"main","sequence":62},{"id":"part_1d6f563e17b4","type":"artifact","artifact_id":"artifact_7eafca35ba22438299cc5cfbf311050a","agent_id":"main","sequence":63}],"run_id":"825e7fe2-000d