urvey ( Digital soil survey and generally is the most detailed level of soil geographic data developed by the National Cooperative Soil Survey ) Soil Survey - 2003 Land Capability - Bailey ( Indicates land capability boundaries within the Lake Tahoe Basin ) Tables: BMP_Status (BMP Certificate and Source Certificate Information) BMP_Site_Constraints (Parcel-level site constraints record in the BMP Database)","endpoint_id":"ndp","endpoint_name":"NDP catalog","id":"f8e23062-bc48-4bdd-9698-374bee3712fd","name":"lake-tahoe","organization":"trpa","resources":[{"format":"HTML","id":"c64ca81e-d6e3-4c93-86d2-4de808bcc9b9","name":"ArcGIS Hub Dataset","path":"1-ArcGIS Hub Dataset","revision":"5ffa34932301cd59809bffe4a3676203e9bd74c9c00ed4cec3e7f4c953b34726","size":0},{"format":"Esri REST","id":"422993e2-1c8f-437b-8327-48f674ef3c01","name":"Esri Rest API","path":"2-Esri Rest API","revision":"bdb140ebb77cc8375ce6d9015ea1b00a7994b7a560d37d83a5461ad50b5fd1a8","size":0},{"format":"GeoJSON","id":"6c62c1d6-bce0-4ee1-bd9c-8b55fd3f1eee","name":"GeoJSON","path":"3-GeoJSON","revision":"83a6f210477aa6ca20392342068ba6d55c93b84d8e887a52df5928eac9ebfb8f","size":0},{"format":"CSV","id":"4b8c97f0-ee3c-4830-aa4a-b9b7b51abb42","name":"CSV","path":"4-CSV","revision":"559f42bd9e39798c347d658581bcf3b08fb6a817fece9766e94d20ccb7cd716e","size":0},{"format":"KML","id":"5a6b335c-537e-4989-9c60-08899d310333","name":"KML","path":"5-KML","revision":"d3bcd74a7c5911b93c13f0c244bd42a0e5bb03a73db38b082c3cd1e8313c5c89","size":0},{"format":"ZIP","id":"57538d23-ed5a-4ef4-826c-1a4e8d9dd33d","name":"Shapefile","path":"6-Shapefile","revision":"8a995271e979332f5641bbefb455019f2e4b16d0eaaa2b5daf914808770dc44e","size":0}],"title":"Lake Tahoe"},{"access":null,"description":"Watershed Sciences, Inc. (WSI) collected Light Detection and Ranging (Lidar) data of land surrounding Lake Tahoe from August 11th to August 24th, 2010 totaling 232,536 acres. The resulting dataset has average first-return density of delivered dataset