s, passes, points, beaches, other named places). USFS Trails - Feature Class created to be used for trail transportation map product display and analysis. Public Access - The California Protected Areas Database (CPAD) contains data on lands owned in fee by governments, non-profits and some private entities that are protected for open space purposes. Data includes all such areas in California, from small urban parks to large national parks and forests, mostly aligned to assessor parcel boundaries. LTBMU Recreation Sites - developed recreation sites that are large enough to be represented as areas or polygons. LTBMU Recreation Opportunity Spectrum - Depicts the spatial location of areas showing the type of Recreation Opportunity Settings that exist. This version of the ROS layer was developed for the 1988 Forest Plan of the Lake Tahoe Basin Management Unit.","endpoint_id":"ndp","endpoint_name":"NDP catalog","id":"e69a0ab4-4b1b-4c43-9ecb-6910124b2b5d","name":"ltbmu-trails","organization":"trpa","resources":[{"format":"HTML","id":"17a982fc-00d3-44c6-8aa2-a5973bf30778","name":"ArcGIS Hub Dataset","path":"1-ArcGIS Hub Dataset","revision":"4ca28580791d2b7c33e0b82a3c28b1b685a49c3dc6aae7f61add59cc8655aa49","size":0},{"format":"Esri REST","id":"37fbdfcf-4f2a-48d0-82a5-7a5429ce7134","name":"Esri Rest API","path":"2-Esri Rest API","revision":"1c0e44b17a9cfd3a153a1d7305b8089e353aa415ee4e7a7669a4b59cef27b152","size":0},{"format":"GeoJSON","id":"99172196-e7cc-4b2d-bacd-8ebc921490e5","name":"GeoJSON","path":"3-GeoJSON","revision":"4ba60d2d4875495bb2bc20cc17cfc36041c89275651a42e99c744a2b4e3ac0f8","size":0},{"format":"CSV","id":"209d13c2-06a0-420a-bf43-d3a12124ca1e","name":"CSV","path":"4-CSV","revision":"8127ce67d54fee669816e2a5b06c1cb7d744cae1000953a961cdabbb0e9ea215","size":0},{"format":"KML","id":"ec0ba256-49e1-4fd1-b511-af57311845a1","name":"KML","path":"5-KML","revision":"0a1cf6115271146b090ecdab5fc14d1d3bd49194b9c39745ae6c91abe886fcf9","size":0},{"format":"ZIP","id":"156f7310-