eted, and do not pass the linked revision to a downloaded read. To read\nthrough the link, open the selected path\nwith `connected_data_open(source_id=SOURCE_ID, path=RELATIVE_PATH, ...)`.\nUse its immutable `resource_id` with\n`workspace_resource_read` or `workspace_resource_inspect`. Linked paths are virtual\nreferences, not shell mounts.\n\n## Materialize and analyze\n\nFor Python or shell analysis use\n`connected_data_download(source_id=SOURCE_ID, selected_paths=[RELATIVE_PATH])`.\nWait for completion and use the returned materialized path. Do not guess a source\nfolder path or resubmit an accepted download. NDP originals stay intact; create\nseparate derivatives in the workspace. A downloaded historical copy is not a\ncurrent upstream read after disconnection.\n\nUse the returned downloaded input path directly for reads, even when CLIO stores\nit outside the workspace root. Shell `access_paths` requests broader folder\npermissions; it is not needed to read these approved inputs and cannot authorize\nwrites to protected source snapshots. Keep scripts, outputs and temporary work\nunder the workspace. If selected measurements lack the necessary coverage, inspect\nalternative resources in the collection before treating that as a collection-wide\ngap. Record exactly which instruments and intervals were examined.\n\nChoose analysis from actual data, not format assumptions:\n\n| Data | Checks before computing |\n| --- | --- |\n| Time series | Measurement time vs capture time, timezone/epoch encoding, cadence, gaps, duplicates, component names and units. GNSS components may differ in scaling and reference frame. |\n| HDF5 / NetCDF / array output | Group/variable names, dimensions, coordinate conventions, units, fill values, chunking and requested subset. Inspect metadata before reading an entire large array. |\n| Spatial/station records | Coordinate reference, channel/network/station identifiers, geometry and station epochs. Metadata rows are not waveform or displacement samples. |\n| Service or stream response | Actual payload schema, status/control events, measurement timestamps and whether data is replay or current acquisition. See `services-and-streams.md`. |\n\nUse existing installed readers and the relevant analysis/visualization skills;\ndon't execute downloaded notebooks or deserialize executable objects merely to\nread measurements. Preserve input dataset/resource IDs, source revision and content\nhashes, query filters, units and transformations with the results. Register useful\nreports, tables and figures as artifacts, and visually inspect figures before\ncalling them reviewed. The user may need only a comparison, not a dashboard.\n\n## Interpret failures\n\n- **No matches:** broaden terms, inspect publisher naming and coverage, then refine.\n  Distinguish an empty successful result from a failed search.\n- **503 / timeout:** preserve the query and actual error; bounded retry or narrower\n  paging can help. Do not report an empty catalog or reconnect the account as a\n  generic remedy for a server outage.\n- **Sign-in required / 401 / 403:** separate saved account state, destination/issuer\n  compatibility and resource/Endpoint authorization. Successful browser SSO alone\n  is not the private CLIO grant.\n- **Only a preview/service link:** explain what it supplies and follow the service\n  route when needed. Do not manufacture a data-file URL from its filename.\n- **Partial download or changed revision:** inspect the accepted task's result and\n  exact source identity. Keep verified files; resolve the changed input before\n  claiming the full selection was analyzed.\n\nFinish with the scientific result, selected collection/coverage and usable output\nartifacts. Separate found metadata, obtained bytes and checked analysis in the\nevidence; none substitutes for the next.\n","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":190.18125534057617,"started_at":"2026-10-19T06:55:42.059771+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T06:55:42.249952+00:00"},{"id":"call_ccedcedff627","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","run_id":"a359ea79-4c95-4063-89a8-f345ed58c687","name":"write_todos","title":"Update Todos","state":"succeeded","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Find and inspect NDP’s Lake Tahoe boundary and its spatial metadata.","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Validate the geometry and compute a defensible surface-area estimate.","status":"pending"},{"content":"Make and visually review a map, and publish the measurement method and results.","status":"pending"}]},"output":"Recorded 3 todo(s): 0 completed, 1 in_progress, 2 pending.","presentation":{"action":"Update Todos","summary":"3 todos changed","blocks":[{"id":"todo-0","type":"check","media_type":"","text":"Find and inspect NDP’s Lake Tahoe boundary and its spatial metadata.","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"state":"in_progress","change":"added","uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"todo-1","type":"check","media_type":"","text":"Validate the geometry and compute a defensible surface-area estimate.","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"state":"pending","change":"added","uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"todo-2","type":"check","media_type":"","text":"Make and visually review a map, and publish the measurement method and results.","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"state":"pending","change":"added","uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":177.19388008117676,"started_at":"2026-10-19T06:55:42.064481+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T06:55:42.241674+00:00"},{"id":"call_ba0dc97f14b7","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","run_id":"a359ea79-4c95-4063-89a8-f345ed58c687","name":"load_skill","title":"Load skill","state":"succeeded","input":{"kwargs":{"file":"","files":null,"skill_id":"connect-data"}},"output":"# Skill: connect-data\nSkill directory (use as SKILL_ROOT): D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\clio-ndp-source\\src\\clio_agent\\gact\\builtin_skills\\connect-data\n# Connect data\n\nStart with supplied attachments, references and the current workspace folders.\nInspect the relevant files and their self-description using available file tools.\nA primary workspace folder is already input; an empty connected-source list\ndoes not mean its files are missing. If a read fails, diagnose the reported\naccess or runtime error rather than asking the user to reconnect that folder.\n\nUse this setup workflow when the user explicitly wants to connect a source,\nor a bounded workspace inspection finds that the needed data is elsewhere.\nExplain what input is missing and ask where it is before requesting setup.\n\nCall `connected_data_status` for the inventory of approved workspace folders,\nattached sources, and signed-in provider accounts. This read returns status,\nnot a setup control. If this tool is absent in a child session, return to the\nmain session for setup.\n\nFor National Data Platform requests, load `work-with-ndp`. Its tools are enabled\nonly when this workspace has a connected NDP dataset or visible saved Endpoint.\nIf absent, direct the user to **Attach > NDP** to select a dataset or connect an\nEndpoint, then continue on the next turn. When enabled, its catalog discovery\ntools resolve organizations, datasets and selected resource IDs before connecting;\ndo not invent the private NDP selection configuration or ask for a URL first.\n\nWhen an account needs sign-in, explain the need in your answer and use its\nreturned `login_action` as an ordinary A2UI Button's action. Load the active\ncatalog for the exact component shape. The user sees and clicks this control\nin the answer; the existing private account flow opens. It never passes a\ncredential to you. Do not bury a requested action only in Activity.\n\nWhen the user asks to attach a remote source, use `connected_data_connect`\nto attach it. A URL alone is not a request to connect a source. A new connection\npasses through the session permission gate;\nbypass can approve it automatically, while explicit deny/ask rules still apply.\nAn already-approved identical source is reused. Registration, authentication\nand a successfully linked file index are separate states: report the returned\nstate honestly. After sign-in, retry connection to build the linked index.\n\nFor ordinary GitHub inspection, releases, cloning and development, use `gh`\nthrough the normal shell and its configured account. The shared GitHub shell\nprompt explains release evidence and stable/prerelease distinctions. Do not\nconnect a source solely because the user provided a repository URL or asked\nfor a public release. Public API/browser reads are also sufficient for public\nfacts when the CLI cannot perform the read.\n\nUse this connected-source workflow when the user wants repository data attached\nto the workspace. Its private CLIO account, repository/folder grants and source\nworking-copy review/publication rules remain independent of ordinary shell work.\n\nBriefly explain that the user selects a source and, when required, signs in in\ntheir browser. Sign-in runs independently of the agent; only the outcome and\napproved data references are returned. The UI's info icon explains this privacy\nboundary. Never ask for passwords, access tokens, authorization codes, callback\nURLs, or OAuth client configuration in chat. Never perform sign-in with shell,\nHTTP, or browser tools, and never read CLIO's private credential files.\n\nWait for the user to complete setup; do not repeatedly poll. Call\n`connected_data_status` again when they return. Report the actual source status;\nregistration alone does not mean files are available. Use the approved local\npath only after materialization is ready. Disconnected sources cannot access\nupstream data; their retained local copies are historical evidence.\n\nRead only is the default. Working copy preserves an immutable baseline and\nrequires the user to review selected changes before applying them upstream.\nWrite enabled is offered only where the selected host supports a genuinely\nwritable folder. Do not substitute synchronization or install filesystem drivers.\nRefresh, apply changes, disconnect, remove a copy, and delete upstream data are\ndifferent actions. Use the trusted UI for permission changes and reviewed writes.\n\nAll paths belong to the connected CLIO named in the picker. To send a desktop\nfolder to a remote CLIO, use **Upload desktop folder** and preserve its structure.\nIf a provider reports that distributor setup is missing, report that prerequisite;\ndo not ask an ordinary user to register an OAuth application.","presentation":{"subject":"skill-name","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"skill-name","type":"text","media_type":"","text":"connect-data","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"content","type":"markdown","media_type":"","text":"Skill directory (use as SKILL_ROOT): D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\clio-ndp-source\\src\\clio_agent\\gact\\builtin_skills\\connect-data\n# Connect data\n\nStart with supplied attachments, references and the current workspace folders.\nInspect the relevant files and their self-description using available file tools.\nA primary workspace folder is already input; an empty connected-source list\ndoes not mean its files are missing. If a read fails, diagnose the reported\naccess or runtime error rather than asking the user to reconnect that folder.\n\nUse this setup workflow when the user explicitly wants to connect a source,\nor a bounded workspace inspection finds that the needed data is elsewhere.\nExplain what input is missing and ask where it is before requesting setup.\n\nCall `connected_data_status` for the inventory of approved workspace folders,\nattached sources, and signed-in provider accounts. This read returns status,\nnot a setup control. If this tool is absent in a child session, return to the\nmain session for setup.\n\nFor National Data Platform requests, load `work-with-ndp`. Its tools are enabled\nonly when this workspace has a connected NDP dataset or visible saved Endpoint.\nIf absent, direct the user to **Attach > NDP** to select a dataset or connect an\nEndpoint, then continue on the next turn. When enabled, its catalog discovery\ntools resolve organizations, datasets and selected resource IDs before connecting;\ndo not invent the private NDP selection configuration or ask for a URL first.\n\nWhen an account needs sign-in, explain the need in your answer and use its\nreturned `login_action` as an ordinary A2UI Button's action. Load the active\ncatalog for the exact component shape. The user sees and clicks this control\nin the answer; the existing private account flow opens. It never passes a\ncredential to you. Do not bury a requested action only in Activity.\n\nWhen the user asks to attach a remote source, use `connected_data_connect`\nto attach it. A URL alone is not a request to connect a source. A new connection\npasses through the session permission gate;\nbypass can approve it automatically, while explicit deny/ask rules still apply.\nAn already-approved identical source is reused. Registration, authentication\nand a successfully linked file index are separate states: report the returned\nstate honestly. After sign-in, retry connection to build the linked index.\n\nFor ordinary GitHub inspection, releases, cloning and development, use `gh`\nthrough the normal shell and its configured account. The shared GitHub shell\nprompt explains release evidence and stable/prerelease distinctions. Do not\nconnect a source solely because the user provided a repository URL or asked\nfor a public release. Public API/browser reads are also sufficient for public\nfacts when the CLI cannot perform the read.\n\nUse this connected-source workflow when the user wants repository data attached\nto the workspace. Its private CLIO account, repository/folder grants and source\nworking-copy review/publication rules remain independent of ordinary shell work.\n\nBriefly explain that the user selects a source and, when required, signs in in\ntheir browser. Sign-in runs independently of the agent; only the outcome and\napproved data references are returned. The UI's info icon explains this privacy\nboundary. Never ask for passwords, access tokens, authorization codes, callback\nURLs, or OAuth client configuration in chat. Never perform sign-in with shell,\nHTTP, or browser tools, and never read CLIO's private credential files.\n\nWait for the user to complete setup; do not repeatedly poll. Call\n`connected_data_status` again when they return. Report the actual source status;\nregistration alone does not mean files are available. Use the approved local\npath only after materialization is ready. Disconnected sources cannot access\nupstream data; their retained local copies are historical evidence.\n\nRead only is the default. Working copy preserves an immutable baseline and\nrequires the user to review selected changes before applying them upstream.\nWrite enabled is offered only where the selected host supports a genuinely\nwritable folder. Do not substitute synchronization or install filesystem drivers.\nRefresh, apply changes, disconnect, remove a copy, and delete upstream data are\ndifferent actions. Use the trusted UI for permission changes and reviewed writes.\n\nAll paths belong to the connected CLIO named in the picker. To send a desktop\nfolder to a remote CLIO, use **Upload desktop folder** and preserve its structure.\nIf a provider reports that distributor setup is missing, report that prerequisite;\ndo not ask an ordinary user to register an OAuth application.","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":93.02115440368652,"started_at":"2026-10-19T06:55:54.964031+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T06:55:55.057052+00:00"},{"id":"call_818318fc4b0d","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","run_id":"a359ea79-4c95-4063-89a8-f345ed58c687","name":"load_skill","title":"Load skill","state":"succeeded","input":{"kwargs":{"file":"","files":null,"skill_id":"review-visual-presentation"}},"output":"# Skill: review-visual-presentation\nSkill directory (use as SKILL_ROOT): D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\clio-ndp-source\\src\\clio_agent\\gact\\builtin_skills\\review-visual-presentation\nUse visual interaction to investigate a question and to improve what a person\nwill see. The loop is: inspect the evidence and current view, change a declared\ncontrol or component, inspect the resulting image, reason, and refine.\nChoose changes that resolve a concrete uncertainty or presentation problem.\nThis applies to maps, charts, tables, images, models and interconnected reports.\n\nFor a substantial authored dashboard or diagram, close this concrete loop:\n\n1. Open the actual published viewer, inspect its current capture target, and\n   capture the overview at the width the person will use.\n2. Look at the returned image, not just its URI, source JSON or tool success.\n   Check whether the main idea is apparent, text is readable, the whole diagram\n   fits, and empty space or narrow columns obscure relationships. Ask whether\n   a full-width view, equal panels or a simpler arrangement would explain it better.\n   Include the surrounding frame/component headings, not only the plotted marks:\n   a title cut off with an ellipsis is a defect even when the graph fits. Check\n   whether labels can actually be read at this size, rather than merely seen.\n3. Identify a concrete defect and change the source or a declared view control.\n   Changing column counts is useful only when it fixes the observed problem.\n4. Capture the revised view and inspect its image to confirm the correction.\n   Check an expanded view as well when the docked and expanded arrangements differ.\n5. Exercise important declared controls or linked selections. For a workflow\n   folder link, verify the target with filesystem tools. If interaction tools are\n   available, check that clicking selects that folder in Files. Claim a navigation\n   check only when it was observed; a highlighted box alone does not prove it.\n\nRepeat while a material defect remains. State the actual visual checks and any\nunresolved limitation. Schema validation, a capture receipt and an uninspected\nimage do not establish visual quality. A small inline diagram does not require\nbuilding a dashboard or following an elaborate layout recipe.\nKeep docked and expanded findings separate: readability in an expanded image\ndoes not establish readability in a narrow pane. When text remains too small,\nrevise the view or state that limitation instead of declaring the review clear.\n\nRead the current surface with `inspect_a2ui_surface` and load the relevant\nactive catalog schemas. `update_a2ui_components` replaces complete definitions\nfor the named components; preserve the other properties, references and links.\n`update_a2ui_data_model` changes a declared binding. Reuse shared filter and\nselection semantics rather than inventing another interaction model. For definition\nchanges to saved dashboards, edit the source document and publish a new immutable version.\n\nDistinguish server state from a rendered view. A producer's `rendered=true`\nmeans the definition was accepted, not that you inspected its pixels.\n`inspect_a2ui_surface` reports fresh mounted viewers, declared bindings,\ncurrent values, cameras, active tabs, data references and readiness. Choose\nthe viewer you mean when several are open. `capture_targets` supplies the exact\ncapture arguments for each visible matching viewer; use the chosen target\nwithout adding a guessed view epoch. Pass the inspected revision to\nupdates, then capture the new revision with `capture_a2ui_surface`. Its result\nattaches real pixels to your next model step and retains a hashed image artifact\nwith the viewer state. For a saved dashboard, pass its immutable `artifact_id`\nto inspection and capture. Review a temporary live surface when you need to\nchange a saved definition; publish the reviewed document as a new version.\nTo navigate or change declared controls in an open saved dashboard, use\n`update_a2ui_data_model` with its `artifact_id`, surface/revision, selected\n`viewer_id` and inspected `expected_view_revision`. This changes only that\nview's local binding. Inspect its acknowledgement and capture the new epoch;\nit does not edit the immutable artifact or submit a question answer.\nBind `Tabs.activeTab` to review each tab; its value is a tab child id.\nBind `clio.map.v1.camera` to pan, zoom or rotate a map, sharing the path when\nviews should move together. Keep reference-backed queries and selections\nauthoritative. An image URI, export link or unrelated earlier screenshot is\nnot visual inspection. Verify the capture's revision and state before reasoning.\nUse the inspected component's exact binding path; map and mesh cameras can\nhave different paths and shapes in the same dashboard. Change that binding\ninstead of replacing the root data model with a guessed set of properties.\nCompare the actual captured camera, frame and filters with the requested\nvalues. If a declared control did not move, inspect its binding and correct\nthe update, then capture again before claiming the change worked.\nIf a viewer is still loading, pass `expected_view_revision=null` (or omit it)\nto let capture wait for readiness within its deadline. Pin a view epoch\nwhen an already-ready human view must match exactly; a loading epoch\nintentionally becomes stale as tiles or layout finish.\nAfter publication, the newly opened viewer can still be mounting. A single\n`a2ui_view_stale` or `a2ui_render_not_ready` result is not the end of the review:\ninspect the same immutable artifact again and retry capture with its current\nviewer. If `ready` is false, pass `expected_view_revision=null` rather than guessing\nzero. Retry at most twice for each requested view; stop and report the actual limitation if the viewer\nis absent or still cannot supply pixels. After each successful declared tab or\ncamera change, use the acknowledged epoch or inspect afresh before capture.\nIf capture or a requested control is unavailable, make supported structural\ncorrections and state the remaining verification limit; do not fabricate a\ncapture or describe a map camera as controllable because the person can zoom it.\n\nInspect at the size the person will use. Check the overview, relevant tabs,\nlabels, legends, units, contrast, clipping, framing and controls. Ask whether\nthe view answers the question and is valuable to a human: can the reader find\nthe important comparison without deciphering a dense wall of marks?\nAlso review the explanation: what conclusion can a person see in this image,\nwhich marks support it, and what uncertainty remains? Compare related panels'\ncategory meanings, ranges, dates and selected records. Use direct labels or\nreference marks where they reduce the effort of finding the evidence. Remove\nredundant panels and give the central comparison more space. Load the dashboard\nskill's `references/report-design.md` when composing a substantial report.\nCheck composition as a whole: can related charts, images, viewports and text\nbe interpreted together without tab switching? Review a whole-report image,\nnot only individual views. Preserve unequal row proportions when expanded\nand readable stacking when docked. Optional tabs must not hide essential\nevidence from the initial view or PNG.\nPerform this review yourself before presenting a complex visual; the person\nshould not need to request a screenshot check separately.\nWhen a view is crowded, show the meaningful subset or aggregate first. Retain\nthe complete source data and explain the initial slice. Make additional series,\nlayers or views available through catalog-supported selectors, filters, tabs\nor optional-view controls, with readable labels and visible inclusion state.\nDo not invent a visibility property or hide contrary evidence to improve the\nstory. Check the revealed detail as well as the quiet default.\n\nUse annotations to point to evidence during explanations and questions.\nUpdate a chart with supported layered marks for a labelled point, red outline,\nrange or trend; keep the original rows and quantitative encodings intact.\nUse real data coordinates or stable entity IDs when a mark should follow\nzoom/filter changes. A pixel-positioned mark belongs to one captured viewport;\ndo not reuse it on a different view as if it still identifies the same data.\nAnnotations clarify evidence; they do not change measurements or submit an\nanswer. `ask_user` continues to own question submission independently.\n\nFor worked decision patterns, load `references/investigation-patterns.md`\nfrom this skill. Stop once the question is resolved and the relevant views\nare readable; further captures should answer a remaining concern. Keep visual\nobservations, calculations and unresolved uncertainty distinct in the answer.\n\nKeep the final response focused on the requested deliverables and findings.\n`capture_a2ui_surface` retains its screenshots as verification evidence; do not\nregister or list each capture as another output. For other review images/PDFs,\nuse `create_artifact(..., purpose=\"verification\")`; working files use\n`purpose=\"intermediate\"`. Both remain accessible in Observability and lineage.\nRequested images/PDFs use `purpose=\"deliverable\"`. When revising an output,\nkeep its artifact family/name; the response presents its latest deliverable\nversion while Versions and Observability retain earlier attempts.\n\nBundled files (use file=... for one or files=[...] for a batch):\n- examples/annotated-scatter.json\n- references/investigation-patterns.md","presentation":{"subject":"skill-name","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"skill-name","type":"text","media_type":"","text":"review-visual-presentation","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""},{"id":"content","type":"markdown","media_type":"","text":"Skill directory (use as SKILL_ROOT): D:\\Libraries\\Documents\\projects\\clio-ndp-source\\src\\clio_agent\\gact\\builtin_skills\\review-visual-presentation\nUse visual interaction to investigate a question and to improve what a person\nwill see. The loop is: inspect the evidence and current view, change a declared\ncontrol or component, inspect the resulting image, reason, and refine.\nChoose changes that resolve a concrete uncertainty or presentation problem.\nThis applies to maps, charts, tables, images, models and interconnected reports.\n\nFor a substantial authored dashboard or diagram, close this concrete loop:\n\n1. Open the actual published viewer, inspect its current capture target, and\n   capture the overview at the width the person will use.\n2. Look at the returned image, not just its URI, source JSON or tool success.\n   Check whether the main idea is apparent, text is readable, the whole diagram\n   fits, and empty space or narrow columns obscure relationships. Ask whether\n   a full-width view, equal panels or a simpler arrangement would explain it better.\n   Include the surrounding frame/component headings, not only the plotted marks:\n   a title cut off with an ellipsis is a defect even when the graph fits. Check\n   whether labels can actually be read at this size, rather than merely seen.\n3. Identify a concrete defect and change the source or a declared view control.\n   Changing column counts is useful only when it fixes the observed problem.\n4. Capture the revised view and inspect its image to confirm the correction.\n   Check an expanded view as well when the docked and expanded arrangements differ.\n5. Exercise important declared controls or linked selections. For a workflow\n   folder link, verify the target with filesystem tools. If interaction tools are\n   available, check that clicking selects that folder in Files. Claim a navigation\n   check only when it was observed; a highlighted box alone does not prove it.\n\nRepeat while a material defect remains. State the actual visual checks and any\nunresolved limitation. Schema validation, a capture receipt and an uninspected\nimage do not establish visual quality. A small inline diagram does not require\nbuilding a dashboard or following an elaborate layout recipe.\nKeep docked and expanded findings separate: readability in an expanded image\ndoes not establish readability in a narrow pane. When text remains too small,\nrevise the view or state that limitation instead of declaring the review clear.\n\nRead the current surface with `inspect_a2ui_surface` and load the relevant\nactive catalog schemas. `update_a2ui_components` replaces complete definitions\nfor the named components; preserve the other properties, references and links.\n`update_a2ui_data_model` changes a declared binding. Reuse shared filter and\nselection semantics rather than inventing another interaction model. For definition\nchanges to saved dashboards, edit the source document and publish a new immutable version.\n\nDistinguish server state from a rendered view. A producer's `rendered=true`\nmeans the definition was accepted, not that you inspected its pixels.\n`inspect_a2ui_surface` reports fresh mounted viewers, declared bindings,\ncurrent values, cameras, active tabs, data refere