tifact://artifact_743fe7c0c0944e3abfcf3d9bb0f16b66","part_id":"live_a2ui_d5075ed1cdf7","rendered":true,"revision":2,"session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","session_surface_ids":["tahoe-boundary-map"],"state":"ready","surface_id":"tahoe-boundary-map"},"presentation":{"action":"Generate widget","subject":"surface","status":"succeeded","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"surface","type":"link","media_type":"","text":"","label":"Map","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"target":"surface","uri":"tahoe-boundary-map","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":529.0868282318115,"started_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:21.699204+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:22.228291+00:00"},{"id":"call_d3ba54aacd97","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","run_id":"a359ea79-4c95-4063-89a8-f345ed58c687","name":"create_artifact","title":"Create Artifact","state":"succeeded","input":{"annotation":"Measurement results, provenance, exact method, cross-checks and interpretation limits for Lake Tahoe boundary area.","artifacts":null,"content":"# Lake Tahoe: area inside the NDP/TRPA boundary\n\n## Result\n\nThe mapped boundary encloses **497.7 km²**, equivalent to **192.2 mi²** or approximately **123,000 acres**. This is a horizontal GIS footprint estimate, not a dated observation of the lake's current water surface. Retained computational digits below are for reproducibility, not a claim of shoreline accuracy.\n\n| Check | Area (km²) |\n|---|---:|\n| Local Lambert azimuthal equal-area polygon | 497.727861084 |\n| WGS84 ellipsoidal geodesic polygon | 497.727861083 |\n| Exact sum of clipped 1 km grid cells | 497.727861084 |\n| Native NAD83 / UTM zone 10N recomputation | 498.136861937 |\n| Source `SHAPESTArea` / 1,000,000 | 498.136781042 |\n\n## Source and meaning\n\nFound in NDP's central catalog: **Lake Tahoe**, publisher **trpa**; dataset `f8e23062-bc48-4bdd-9698-374bee3712fd`, GeoJSON resource `6c62c1d6-bce0-4ee1-bd9c-8b55fd3f1eee`. Retrieved 19 October 2026.\n\nThe publisher's [ArcGIS layer 1](https://maps.trpa.org/server/rest/services/Datadownloader_SoilsandHydro/MapServer/1) describes it as “Lake Tahoe boundary delineation.” The [Hub record](https://data-trpa.opendata.arcgis.com/datasets/9d7ae4b852254684bd310c68b98b3772_1) is the NDP-listed landing page. This is not a basin/jurisdiction boundary and is not the separate high-water-line layer.\n\nThe GeoJSON declares `urn:ogc:def:crs:OGC:1.3:CRS84`: WGS84 coordinates in longitude, latitude order. The publisher layer's native extent is in EPSG:26910 (NAD83 / UTM zone 10N). Its [metadata XML](https://maps.trpa.org/server/rest/services/Datadownloader_SoilsandHydro/MapServer/1/metadata) has an Esri creation date of 2021-12-20, but supplies no shoreline survey date, water-level reference, or positional accuracy. That metadata date is not treated as a measurement date.\n\nInput SHA-256: `bf1d07bac1af2b520ba21963b30048f1f8231c8882b86f8923b3f963ca641154`.\n\n## Measurement procedure\n\n1. Read the complete GeoJSON: one feature, `OBJECTID=410`, one valid Polygon, 20,472 exterior-ring coordinates including closure, no interior rings. No invalid-geometry repair, smoothing, simplification, or added shoreline vertices was used. Bounds: longitude -120.1639971 to -119.9260837; latitude 38.9366087 to 39.2489925 degrees.\n2. Transform all longitude/latitude vertices with `always_xy=True` to a local Lambert azimuthal equal-area projection in metres: `+proj=laea +lat_0=39.1 +lon_0=-120 +datum=WGS84 +units=m`. This avoids treating degrees squared or Web Mercator screen area as surface area.\n3. Compute planar polygon area from the projected ring (shoelace algorithm), subtracting encoded holes if present. Here there are none. Area = 497,727,861.0836794 m². Divide by 1,000,000 for km², 2,589,988.110336 for mi², and 4,046.8564224 for acres.\n4. Independently cross-check the same ring using `pyproj.Geod(ellps='WGS84').geometry_area_perimeter`, with counterclockwise exterior orientation. Absolute area = 497,727,861.08309984 m². Difference from equal-area result = 0.00058 m². This checks projection/numerics, not boundary truth.\n5. To illustrate area on the map, intersect the polygon with each 1,000 m × 1,000 m projected grid square and sum the exact intersections. **429 full cells + 68.727861 km² across 143 partial cells = 497.727861 km².** Partial shore cells are clipped, not rounded to whole squares. The grid is a decomposition of the polygon, not a pixel-count approximation.\n\nThe source area attribute is about 0.409 km² (0.082%) larger than the equal-area result and is consistent with a native projected area: recomputation in EPSG:26910 gives 498.136862 km². UTM is not equal-area. The source attribute was therefore retained for comparison, not used as the lake-area estimate.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- This boundary can estimate the lake's mapped horizontal footprint, but cannot establish today's surface area or area at a particular lake elevation without a dated/reference-level shoreline.\n- The polygon encodes no holes. No independent island inventory was used or subtracted; land omitted from the encoded geometry may be counted.\n- Shoreline mapping resolution and positional accuracy are unspecified. Numerical agreement between methods is not an uncertainty interval.\n- Calculations refer to WGS84's reference ellipsoid; no elevation adjustment or three-dimensional wave/surface-area calculation was made. No bathymetry or volume was inferred.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nPython 3.14.8, Shapely 2.2.0, pyproj 3.8.0; Matplotlib used for the figure. The companion calculation package retains the exact source boundary, metadata, result JSON, clipped-cell CSV and saved calculation/map script. The interactive GeoJSON is the same geometry (ring orientation normalized) with area/description properties added. The downloadable map uses local equal-area coordinates; its green background is context only, not a separate land-cover dataset.\n","kind":"report","name":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-20261019\\tahoe-boundary-18\\tahoe-area\\measurement_method.md","path":"","pdf_preview":null,"purpose":"deliverable","used":["artifact_47ed32665c174a5daf93ef98517023fc","res_d3315fbfc31c4c7b97d82939c558ef45","D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-20261019\\tahoe-boundary-18\\tahoe-area\\measurement.json","https://maps.trpa.org/server/rest/services/Datadownloader_SoilsandHydro/MapServer/1/metadata"]},"output":{"artifacts":[{"accepted":true,"artifact_id":"artifact_22bf7ec3fa6249398f8450df246ba997","created":true,"custody":"cas","kind":"report","mechanism":"model","name":"measurement_method.md","reason":"","sha256":"7e75bf745b98af37f09659f971b33104a5943633d9c3061cc424ee7d47eadad3","version":1}],"created":1,"deduplicated":0,"pdf_previews":[],"promotion_budget":{"limit":8,"remaining":5,"used":3},"rejected":0},"presentation":{"action":"Create Artifact","subject":"artifact-0","summary":"Created version 1","blocks":[{"id":"artifact-0","type":"link","media_type":"","text":"","label":"measurement_method.md","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"target":"artifact","uri":"artifact_22bf7ec3fa6249398f8450df246ba997","command":"","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":""}]},"duration_ms":570.3046321868896,"started_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:21.839111+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:22.409415+00:00"},{"id":"call_613e2af0538e","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","run_id":"a359ea79-4c95-4063-89a8-f345ed58c687","name":"inspect_a2ui_surface","title":"Inspect widget","state":"succeeded","input":{"artifact_id":"","surface_id":"tahoe-boundary-map"},"output":{"artifact_id":"","capture_targets":[{"artifact_id":"","expected_revision":2,"expected_view_revision":10,"surface_id":"tahoe-boundary-map","viewer_id":"e1b96773-dd3b-441f-8a08-25fede1dc9a6"}],"catalog_id":"https://iowarp.ai/a2ui/catalogs/clio-workspace/v1","components":[{"component":"clio.map.v1","detailField":"detail","geojsonUri":