oken, basemap service or live source download is needed. Source bytes and all numerical inputs are included.\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. Extract the complete ZIP. Keep its folder structure.\n2. Open a terminal in the extracted `tahoe-reproducibility` folder.\n3. With Python 3.14 and uv available, run:\n\n```text\nuv run --isolated --no-project --python 3.14 --with-requirements requirements.lock.txt python verify.py\n```\n\nFor a system without uv, create a virtual environment, activate it, then:\n\n```text\npython -m pip install -r requirements.lock.txt\npython verify.py\n```\n\nInstall dependencies only in that environment. Python 3.14.8 on Windows x86-64 is the tested baseline. Linux/macOS have not been tested. The pins are exact resolved versions, not a bundled interpreter or wheelhouse; first-time setup needs package-index access or a separately prepared wheel cache. Once installed, analysis is offline and PROJ network access is disabled. The dependency lock pins versions but does not include wheel hashes.\n\n## Read without running\n\nOpen `report.html` in a browser for both figures and the complete shoreline table. It uses local files only; there is no JavaScript or CDN. PNGs open in ordinary image viewers, CSVs in spreadsheets, GeoJSON in GIS software, and Markdown methods in a text/Markdown viewer. Opening files in every possible desktop application is not guaranteed by format validation.\n\n## Contents\n\n- `source/`: exact original GeoJSON, publisher layer JSON/XML, IDs, retrieval date, source SHA-256 and attribution.\n- `expected/area/`: original area outputs, exact clipped-cell CSV and map.\n- `expected/shoreline/`: full-precision ten-resolution table, all simplified shorelines, JSON results and detail figure.\n- `methods/`: complete scientific procedures, projections, units and limitations.\n- `scripts/area.py`, `scripts/shoreline.py`: portable Python analyses using paths relative to this package.\n- `verify.py`: integrity, file-opening and numerical regres