\nAlgorithm       Hash                                                                   Path\n---------       ----                                                                   ----\nSHA256          90AA71A46D024BFDA17CFE954DFBF6FAFDDB8A8BA74E46321CED798AD861F158       D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-2.\n\nstatus           : PASS\nmanifest_files   : 26\nopened_files     : 27\ngenerated_opened : 9\nchecks           : 2851\n\n\n","stdout_truncated":false,"timed_out":false,"timeout_s":0.0}},"presentation":{"action":"Run","summary":"","blocks":[{"id":"terminal","type":"terminal","media_type":"","text":"\nAlgorithm       Hash                                                                   Path\n---------       ----                                                                   ----\nSHA256          90AA71A46D024BFDA17CFE954DFBF6FAFDDB8A8BA74E46321CED798AD861F158       D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-2.\n\nstatus           : PASS\nmanifest_files   : 26\nopened_files     : 27\ngenerated_opened : 9\nchecks           : 2851\n\n\n","label":"","language":"","workspace_id":"","path":"","sha256":"","pages":[],"uri":"","command":"$root='D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-20261019\\tahoe-boundary-18'; $p=Join-Path $root '.tmp\\clio-documents\\tahoe\\clean extract 02\\tahoe-reproducibility\\verification\\verification_report.json'; $r=Get-Content -Raw -Encoding utf8 $p | ConvertFrom-Json; Get-FileHash 'tahoe_reproducibility_bundle.zip'; [pscustomobject]@{status=$r.status;manifest_files=$r.manifest_files_verified;opened_files=$r.files_opened.Count;generated_opened=$r.generated_files_opened.Count;checks=$r.checks_passed}; Copy-Item $p 'tahoe_reproducibility_final_test.json'","timed_out":false,"status":"","detail":"","items":[],"action_label":"","exit_code":0}]},"duration_ms":1446.4142322540283,"started_at":"2026-10-19T07:23:03.996603+00:00","completed_at":"2026-10-19T07:23:05.443017+00:00"},{"id":"call_de224c21bee3","session_id":"sess_9cca40f4085e","run_id":"825e7fe2-000d-4768-815b-e022be022f63","name":"create_artifact","title":"Create Artifact","state":"succeeded","input":{"annotation":"","artifacts":[{"annotation":"Standalone source-and-analysis package for both Lake Tahoe area and shoreline-detail comparisons. Final ZIP CRC-tested, re-extracted and rerun in isolated offline Python; all numerical outputs match and both figures are pixel-identical on tested Windows host.","kind":"dataset","name":"tahoe_reproducibility_bundle.zip","path":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-20261019\\tahoe-boundary-18\\tahoe_reproducibility_bundle.zip","purpose":"deliverable"},{"annotation":"Human-readable verification of the exact released ZIP, with hash, environment, file checks, numerical and image results, instructions and portability limits.","content":"# Lake Tahoe standalone reproducibility verification\n\n**Final status: PASS.** The exact released ZIP was extracted into a fresh directory with spaces in its name, then both analyses were rerun using only the extracted files and an isolated Python environment. No CLIO Python package was installed. No NDP login, token, live source download or map service was used. uv offline mode used the already populated dependency cache; PROJ network access was OFF.\n\n## Deliverable identity\n\n- Archive: `tahoe_reproducibility_bundle.zip`\n- Size: 1,342,078 bytes (approximately 1.34 MB).\n- SHA-256: `90aa71a46d024bfda17cfe954dfbf6fafddb8a8ba74e46321ced798ad861f158`\n- 27 package files; 26 SHA-256 manifest entries. The manifest excludes its own bytes.\n- Original boundary SHA-256: `bf1d07bac1af2b520ba21963b30048f1f8231c8882b86f8923b3f963ca641154`.\n\n## Checks performed on the final archive\n\n| Check | Observed result |\n|---|---|\n| ZIP CRC and extraction | Passed |\n| Manifest hashes and original-source identity | All 26 entries matched |\n| Source/derived GeoJSON, JSON, XML | Parsed; GeoJSON features valid and nonempty |\n| CSV files | Opened with consistent column counts; 572 area-cell rows and 10 shoreline-resolution rows |\n| PNG files | Fully decoded at 1440 x 800 and 1600 x 640 pixels |\n| Python files and text methods | UTF-8 read and Python AST validation passed; analysis paths are package-relative |\n| Local HTML report | Parsed; linked local images and method/provenance files exist; no JavaScript/CDN required |\n| Area analysis | Exit code 0; equal-area result 497.727861 km^2 reproduced |\n| Shoreline comparison | Exit code 0; all ten tolerances reproduced, including 123.049623 km original and 101.999834 km at 1,000 m |\n| Area and shoreline CSV numeric differences | Maximum absolute difference 0.0 |\n| Output geometry coordinate differences | Maximum absolute difference 0.0 degrees |\n| Regenerated figures | Both pixel-identical to supplied expected PNGs |\n| Overall automated checks | 2,851 passed |\n\nThe verifier also opened all nine newly generated result files. Figures from the clean rerun were visually inspected and matched the earlier reviewed figures. The retained first-run machine-readable report and logs are inside `validation/`; the final archive was independently re-extracted and retested after adding that evidence. New users generate their own `verification/verification_report.json`.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nExtract the complete ZIP, enter its `tahoe-reproducibility` folder, then run:\n\n```text\nuv run --isolated --no-project --python 3.14 --with-requirements requirements.lock.txt python verify.py\n```\n\nThe README also provides a pip/virtual-environment route. Success prints `\"status\": \"PASS\"` and creates regenerated results in `rerun/`, a `rerun_report.html`, and logs plus the test report under `verification/`. To view the supplied results without running anything, open `report.html`.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nTested: **Python 3.14.8, Windows 11 x86-64**, Shapely 2.2.0, pyproj 3.8.0, GEOS 3.14.1, PROJ 9.8.1, Matplotlib 3.11.2, and the fourteen pinned dependencies recorded in the package. Linux/macOS and GUI opening in Excel/QGIS/browser applications were not tested; the file-opening checks are format parsing, image decoding and local-link validation. Cross-platform plot rasterization can differ even when the numerical tests pass.\n\nThe package contains source data and version pins, **not** an interpreter or a wheelhouse. A colleague's initial dependency installation needs network access or a prepared package cache; analysis itself is offline afterward. Dependency versions are pinned, but wheel hashes are not supplied. Library deprecation warnings were retained in logs and did not prevent either rerun.\n\nNumerical comparison policy is documented in the README and verifier: JSON/CSV absolute tolerance 1e-6 plus relative tolerance 1e-10; geometry coordinates within 1e-10 degrees; counts/text exact. Software metadata is recorded separately. Both PNGs must decode with matching dimensions; cross-platform pixel identity is reported rather than required. On this test host all compared numbers and pixels matched exactly.\n\nScientific caveats remain unchanged: mapped horizontal boundary, not a dated current-water-level survey; no encoded island holes; unknown positional accuracy; simplification tolerance is not pixel size or a statistical uncertainty interval. TRPA attribution, NDP identifiers and publisher URLs are retained. The inspected metadata did not establish additional redistribution licence terms, so no broader source-data licence is asserted.\n","kind":"report","name":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-20261019\\tahoe-boundary-18\\tahoe_reproducibility_verification.md","purpose":"deliverable"},{"annotation":"Actual machine-readable report from the second fresh extraction and isolated offline rerun of the final released ZIP.","kind":"report","name":"tahoe_reproducibility_final_test.json","path":"D:\\CLIO-Develop\\ndp-shareable-20261019\\tahoe-boundary-18\\tahoe_reproducibility_final_test.json","purpose":"verification"}],"content":"","kind":"","name":"","path":"","pdf_preview":null,"purpose":"deliverable","used"